{"title":"2025 IMO Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A <i>proper divisor</i> of a positive integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> other than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" /> itself.\n</p><p>The infinite sequence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cdf697be1e2fbf30c3a7969525a6f643ded3dc5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,\\dots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"70\" height=\"11\" /> consists of positive integers, each of which has at least three proper divisors. For each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/0/340797a8fa9f1a06b10ce9e764998830b15ca755.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n\\ge1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"14\" />, the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/c/36cfb07e4911e7b4f994b858f3d47604ddbee438.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{n+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"33\" height=\"12\" /> is the sum of the three largest proper divisors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/1/6f1a2b6b7c193f9ba2b2134a59f1da5addcfbc98.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"20\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Determine all possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The possible <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" />'s are those with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f43a03db28c623ece3801ba173cebb1b8f993d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_2(a_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76e2997363c38544c8266423b4002aedf5e356ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_3(a_1) &gt; (\\text{ord}_2(a_1)-1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec3d86636b2749c0f2603b1fafdc8376c068fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\nmid a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />. This is straightforward to see from the following claims: For all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fb2585b75fe5ed5004d6dd69053f5929db216c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} &amp;\\text{(i): } 2|a_k \\\\ &amp;\\text{(ii): } \\text{If } 3 \\nmid a_k \\text{ then } a_{k+1} &lt; a_k \\\\ &amp;\\text{(iii): } \\text{If } 3 \\nmid a_k \\text{ then } 3 \\nmid a_{k+1} \\\\  &amp;\\text{(iv): } 3|a_k \\\\ &amp;\\text{(v): } \\text{If } \\text{ord}_2(a_k) \\geq 2 \\text{ and } 3|a_k \\text{ then } \\text{ord}_2(a_{k+1}) = \\text{ord}_2(a_k)-2 \\text{ and } \\text{ord}_3(a_{k+1}) = \\text{ord}_3(a_k)-1 \\\\  &amp;\\text{(vi): } \\text{If } \\text{ord}_2(a_k) = 1 \\text{ and } a_{k+1} = \\frac{a_k}{2} + \\frac{a_k}{m} + \\frac{a_k}{m&#39;} \\text{ then } m \\text{ and } m&#39; \\text{ cannot both be odd} \\end{align*}\" width=\"693\" height=\"158\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/e/afef9f10dfa91a3d7def7c6c726df4ea2acc508e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Proof of (i):}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"102\" height=\"18\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> was odd note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/b/51bb8f97be092c275f4636c0782c3b93b3c69df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> is odd. Furthermore that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ead66d01361f2a3a2d5bc64244d7eae64d20eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} \\leq \\frac{a_k}{3} + \\frac{a_k}{5} + \\frac{a_k}{7} &lt; a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"212\" height=\"34\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/6/1e60e853da9c9b90a2e74e19b3d6f63105fe5294.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1,a_2,...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"67\" height=\"13\" /> would decrease indefinitely.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/e/7ae1176a5f0d9aff154c71c4613ff5f85fe4bf41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Proof of (ii):}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> Note <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/f/a7fc78f230f1f30160efadb15906ad271f23aaa0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} \\leq \\frac{a_k}{2} + \\frac{a_k}{4} + \\frac{a_k}{5} &lt; a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"212\" height=\"34\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/2/7f2032e6940779c22f514cf4d1299b355bf9f7c5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Proof of (vi):}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644b1d79ecab35999ad2f46649f0676cd91d1af5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> are both odd then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/b/51bb8f97be092c275f4636c0782c3b93b3c69df8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"12\" /> is odd, contradicting (i).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/7/c37561898cb3261f0e79ce5cdafa865d0a70c33f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Proof of (iii):}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/f/0afc43ada297093f3a5f6f4d3092574ba08ebc26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4 | a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"34\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/0/d70ef7edd38265ca354e134f5f7100e69306cc04.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} = \\frac{a_k}{2} + \\frac{a_k}{4} + \\frac{a_k}{m} = a_k \\frac{3m+4}{4m}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"273\" height=\"38\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/1/f21b49d4a1d07db0896300cd7c894fdbb50883a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m \\in \\mathbb{N}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"50\" height=\"13\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/b/7dbbd6ef2e770bf8dd57d4b830d5951716090c9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3m+4 \\equiv 1 \\mod 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"154\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295a64e6694214543ee3c9d1eaae45ffc49a0c7c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\nmid a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"44\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef67e9ced545d1f4602b0b6a1bd79ada81efb95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\nmid a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />. Otherwise if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/898691f236e171b92f92113d6f73a2453164627a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_2(a_k) = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" /> (<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/f/f2f02c9865fac2e5074284f54f93fc0fc30edaad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_2(a_k) &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"99\" height=\"20\" /> by (i)) then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/4/644b1d79ecab35999ad2f46649f0676cd91d1af5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&#39;$\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> is even by (vi). WLOG say <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/2/f/b2faa3e881583e5041713bc97941f2c8f212bfd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m&#39; = 2l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"62\" height=\"16\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/2/9b25f8e64b484493fda944d25cad453423041fe6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$l$\" width=\"5\" height=\"12\" /> is a smaller divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/bea4d576937a04ec200b1037fc8ee33e8f744cb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/4/1a40f8faeab3899443c5ea0672d4899be44aa7ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2l$\" width=\"14\" height=\"12\" />, apparently <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/4/204f51af5a6af437ba6c651f90de7a1d498ea29c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m = l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"48\" height=\"14\" />. Hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/d/1/9d1fb9f41e2663e67aed8d4b1084d25acde1b68b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} = \\frac{a_k}{2} + \\frac{a_k}{l} + \\frac{a_k}{2l} = a_k \\frac{3+l}{2l}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"254\" height=\"39\" />. Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/5/6b5848a4e13d5d1a6e8f4a525e8aa4aa449bb85d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\nmid a_k \\implies 3\\nmid l$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"123\" height=\"20\" />. Thus <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/f/bef67e9ced545d1f4602b0b6a1bd79ada81efb95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3 \\nmid a_{k+1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"61\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/e/73ef76516eb91de436d9edd4f690da49c07644a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Proof of (iv):}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"112\" height=\"18\" /> This follows immediately by (ii) and (iii).\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/2/ac240ad9929aad4d3bda7fc3b503b2fb5af9c984.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{Proof of (v):}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"107\" height=\"18\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/c/55c3820a70cfa611efd1d06d862de63be3473a70.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} = \\frac{a_k}{2} + \\frac{a_k}{3} + \\frac{a_k}{4} = a_k \\frac{13}{12}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"235\" height=\"38\" /> as desired. \n</p><p>This concludes the proof of the claims. Now, its apparent <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/b/1ab39d761413804680d26d972381f028001562f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"19\" height=\"13\" /> must be of the form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/8/2980c1d5db1b5c1069bdcbe04058888fac5463e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2^x 3^y z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"46\" height=\"14\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/5/e1528f205a2d68d160c0ad20ee71bba425362345.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2,3 \\nmid z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0517387c7374eb6cfeae1fb2084bf2b52a7303.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y &gt; 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, and that each successive term in the sequence decreases <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, until eventually <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> reaches <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> (not <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />; that would contradict (i)). That is, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c31b6e3f0f5977fc7987d3e0d8bb3ee7c877e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_2{(a_{k_0})} = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" /> for some <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/3/8a3442cf6fbd24badb75194f50de3d80afaf8f7d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k_0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"15\" />. Necessarily <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is odd and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/a/9ca6a6305470e7c6a010c8556b1a9fdbdd08c807.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y &gt; (x-1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> (if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/f/c/7fcd5b6b88720b271de6e10ae982a61a3b2f4e4d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = (x-1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"110\" height=\"20\" /> then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a4b363284d789db88b66cee3cfb025c0dddd4c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_3(a_{k_0}) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"105\" height=\"20\" />, contradicting (iv)). If now <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/6/a/46a62bfcaf6b79640feee79a4fe08cfe7cda6de9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\mid a_{k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" /> then \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/4/2/c42c43607fe0bf39024eb06953bf1b82f8e5af68.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[a_{k_0} = \\frac{a_{k_0}}{2} + \\frac{a_{k_0}}{3} + \\frac{a_{k_0}}{5}\\]\" width=\"174\" height=\"32\" />\ncontradicting (vi). So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/1/d31d718f605a328ae1b5e47e9be8d1a9fa1097dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\nmid a_{k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"50\" height=\"20\" />, which is clearly iff <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec3d86636b2749c0f2603b1fafdc8376c068fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\nmid a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" /> since at no point in the sequence before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/c/75c495692ddc0eb57da9cf723572d0c2d3fee54a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k_0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"26\" height=\"14\" /> can a term be divided by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. In summary, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/4/3f43a03db28c623ece3801ba173cebb1b8f993d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_2(a_1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"65\" height=\"20\" /> is odd, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/e/76e2997363c38544c8266423b4002aedf5e356ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\text{ord}_3(a_1) &gt; (\\text{ord}_2(a_1)-1)/2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"215\" height=\"20\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/c/8ec3d86636b2749c0f2603b1fafdc8376c068fed.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5 \\nmid a_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"43\" height=\"20\" />. On the other hand these properties are sufficient. \n</p><p>~not_detriti\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2025_IMO\" title=\"2025 IMO\">2025 IMO</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions,_with_authors\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"IMO Problems and S